 {2019}\n}\n\n@Inproceedings{Rizvi2026BayesianBF,\n author = {Arshique Rizvi and R. Singh},\n title = {Bayesian Bradley-Terry Framework for Ranking Multi-Indicator Entities: Application to Indian States and Union Territories},\n year = {2026}\n}\n\n@Inproceedings{Broderick2020AnAF,\n author = {Tamara Broderick and Ryan Giordano and R. Meager},\n title = {An Automatic Finite-Sample Robustness Metric: When Can Dropping a Little Data Make a Big Difference?},\n year = {2020}\n}\nsource_evidence\nsource_evidence/downstream\nsource_evidence/downstream/baseline\nsource_evidence/downstream/program\nsource_evidence/downstream/baseline/src\nsource_evidence/downstream/baseline/program_spec.toml\nsource_evidence/downstream/baseline/src/program.py\nsource_evidence/downstream/program/src\nsource_evidence/downstream/program/program_spec.toml\nsource_evidence/downstream/program/src/datasets_offline.py\nsource_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py\n\n- Reference query plan (2026-11-11): wrote 10 queries on Bradley-Terry, AMIP/influence-based data-dropping robustness, Arena/MT-Bench/NBA-Elo data context, vote rigging, leaderboard illusion, rank-aggregation robustness, ranking uncertainty. Chosen over generic benchmarking/optimization queries because they match methods and datasets actually run; no query targets the withheld paper.\n\n- Paper strategy (2026-11-11): chose a thesis-first measurement paper on refit-verified removal budgets for BT leaderboards (crowd vs sports final, expert search-only). Rejected method-superiority (selected == influence-only B2 on all 4 final cases; search delta 0.0, 3/3 scored) and run-diary framings. Final outcome qualified is reported as achieved, not as superiority. Gap noted: references.bib lacks Arena/MT-Bench/influence/rigging entries.\n{\n  \"global_memory_dir\": \"work/results/t06/claude/20261111_064241/investigation\",\n  \"output_dir\": \"work/results/t06/claude/20261111_064241/paper\",\n  \"results_dir\": \"work/results/t06/claude/202611