{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W3sB4FXHeaDTTSWFfuH7T1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Influence-guided minimal-removal search for Bradley-Terry leaderboard rank flips.\n2\t\n3\tThe evaluator calls ``handle(request) -> response`` once per operation with finite JSON values.\n4\tOne episode is: ``reset`` -> ``load_chunk`` x n_chunks -> ``analyze``. Every request is a dict with\n5\tan ``op`` key; every response is a dict. All state lives in this process's memory. The evaluator\n6\tand this process share no filesystem; never rely on paths.\n7\t\n8\tOperations\n9\t----------\n10\t{\"op\": \"reset\", \"seed\": int}\n11\t    Clear ALL state (table, caches, RNG) and seed the RNG. Response: exactly {\"ok\": true}.\n12\t\n13\t{\"op\": \"load_chunk\", \"chunk_index\": int, \"n_chunks\": int, \"n_rows_total\": int, \"n_models\": int,\n14\t \"a\": ARR, \"b\": ARR, \"y\": ARR}\n15\t    One slice of the comparison table (in order, <= 65536 rows per chunk, <= 4 chunks). Row j is\n16\t    \"model a[j] vs model b[j]\" with outcome y[j]: 0 = A wins, 1 = B wins, 2 = tie. ARR =\n17\t    {\"dtype\": \"uint16\" | \"uint8\", \"shape\": [n], \"encoding\": \"base64-le\", \"data\": <base64>}.\n18\t    Response: exactly {\"ok\": true}.\n19\t\n20\t{\"op\": \"analyze\", \"hi\": int, \"lo\": int, \"k_cap\": int, \"tie_as_half_win\": true, \"ridge\": float,\n21\t \"deadline_seconds\": float}\n22\t    Bradley-Terry logistic MLE with ridge; ``hi`` is ranked directly above ``lo``. Propose at most\n23\t    ``k_cap`` unique row indices whose removal makes the exact refit rank ``lo`` strictly above\n24\t    ``hi``. Score = 1 - k / k_cap if the refit flips, else 0.\n25\t    Response: {\"removed\": {\"dtype\": \"uint32\", \"shape\": [k], \"encoding\": \"base64-le\", \"data\": ...},\n26\t    \"diagnostics\": {<name>: <finite number>, ...}}  (optional, <= 32 numbers, ignored for scoring).\n27\t\n28\tMethod (this candidate)\n29\t-----------------------\n30\t1. ``fit_bradley_terry``: damped Newton with analytic gradient / dense Hessian.\n31\t2. ``influence_on_gap``: one-step Newton (influence-function) effect of deleting each row on the\n32\t   gap theta_hi - theta_lo, with the leave-one-out leverage correction 1/(1 - w_i x_i' H^-1 x_i).\n33\t3. ``greedy_flip_budget``: (a) one-shot influence ranking + refit-verified prefix bisection;\n34\t   (b) re-linearised greedy: after every batch refit and recompute influences, batch size = a\n35\t   fraction of the linearised remaining need (Newton-like geometric convergence), then prefix\n36\t   bisection over insertion order; (c) polish by drop-and-readd local search (drop the least useful\n37\t   rows of the incumbent, re-run (b) with a strictly smaller size limit).\n38\t4. ``verify_by_refit``: every candidate set is accepted only after an exact refit flips the pair by\n39\t   a small safety margin. ``random_removal_baseline`` is the random-removal control (diagnostic only).\n40\t\"\"\"\n41\timport base64\n42\timport math\n43\timport time\n44\t\n45\timport numpy as np\n46\t\n47\t_STATE = {}\n48\t\n49\tMARGIN = 1e-5  # safety margin on theta_lo - theta_hi in our own exact refit\n50\tSHRINK = 0.6  # fraction of the linearised need removed per re-linearised round\n51\t\n52\t\n53\tdef _fresh(seed):\n54\t    return {\"seed\": int(seed), \"rng\": np.random.default_rng(int(seed)), \"chunks\": [], \"n_chunks\": None,\n55\t            \"n_rows\": None, \"n_models\": None}\n56\t\n57\t\n58\tdef _decode(arr, dtype, n_expected=None):\n59\t    if (type(arr) is not dict or arr.get(\"encoding\") != \"base64-le\" or arr.get(\"dtype\") != np.dtype(dtype).name):\n60\t        raise ValueError(\"bad array\")\n61\t    out = np.frombuffer(base64.b64decode(arr[\"data\"]), dtype=np.dtype(dtype).newbyteorder(\"<\"))\n62\t    if list(arr[\"shape\"]) != [len(out)] or (n_expected is not None and len(out) != n_expected):\n63\t        raise ValueError(\"bad shape\")\n64\t    return out\n65\t\n66\t\n67\tdef _encode_u32(idx):\n68\t    idx = np.asarray(idx, dtype=\"<u4\")\n69\t    return {\"dtype\": \"uint32\", \"shape\": [int(len(idx))], \"encoding\": \"base64-le\",\n70\t            \"data\": base64.b64encode(idx.tobytes()).decode(\"ascii\")}\n71\t\n72\t\n73\tdef _scores(y):\n74\t    return np.where(y == 0, 1.0, np.where(y == 1, 0.0, 0.5))\n75\t\n76\t\n77\tdef _hessian(a, b, w, m, ridge):\n78\t    h = np.bincount(a * m + b, w, m * m).reshape(m, m)\n79\t    h = -(h + h.T)\n80\t    h[np.diag_indices(m)] += np.bincount(a, w, m) + np.bincount(b, w, m) + ridge\n81\t    return h\n82\t\n83\t\n84\tdef fit_bradley_terry(a, b, s, m, ridge, theta0=None, tol=1e-9, max_iter=60):\n85\t    \"\"\"Ridge-regularised Bradley-Terry MLE (ties = half wins via s) by damped Newton.\"\"\"\n86\t    th = np.zeros(m) if theta0 is None else theta0.copy()\n87\t\n88\t    def obj(t):\n89\t        d = t[a] - t[b]\n90\t        return float(np.sum(np.logaddexp(0.0, d) - s * d) + 0.5 * ridge * float(t @ t))\n91\t\n92\t    f = obj(th)\n93\t    for _ in range(max_iter):\n94\t        p = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-(th[a] - th[b])))\n95\t        r = p - s\n96\t        g = np.bincount(a, r, m) - np.bincount(b, r, m) + ridge * th\n97\t        if np.max(np.abs(g)) < tol:\n98\t            break\n99\t        h = _hessian(a, b, p * (1.0 - p), m, ridge)\n100\t        step = np.linalg.solve(h, g)\n101\t        t = 1.0\n102\t        while True:\n103\t            fn = obj(th - t * step)\n104\t            if fn <= f + 1e-12 * abs(f) or t < 1e-6:\n105\t                break\n106\t            t *= 0.5\n107\t        th = th - t * step\n108\t        f = fn\n109\t    return th\n110\t\n111\t\n112\tdef influence_on_gap(a, b, s, theta, hi, lo, m, ridge, leverage=True):\n113\t    \"\"\"Newton-step change of theta[hi]-theta[lo] if each row were deleted (negative closes the gap).\"\"\"\n114\t    p = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-(theta[a] - theta[b])))\n115\t    w = p * (1.0 - p)\n116\t    h = _hessian(a, b, w, m, ridge)\n117\t    e = np.zeros(m)\n118\t    e[hi], e[lo] = 1.0, -1.0\n119\t    if leverage:\n120\t        hinv = np.linalg.inv(h)\n121\t        v = hinv @ e\n122\t        d = np.diag(hinv)\n123\t        q = d[a] + d[b] - 2.0 * hinv[a, b]\n124\t        den = np.maximum(1.0 - w * q, 1e-3)\n125\t    else:\n126\t        v = np.linalg.solve(h, e)\n127\t        den = 1.0\n128\t    return (p - s) * (v[a] - v[b]) / den\n129\t\n130\t\n131\tdef verify_by_refit(ctx, removed, theta_start=None):\n132\t    \"\"\"Exact refit without ``removed``; returns (flipped, margin = theta_lo - theta_hi, theta).\"\"\"\n133\t    ctx[\"refits\"] += 1\n134\t    keep = np.ones(ctx[\"n\"], bool)\n135\t    if len(removed):\n136\t        keep[np.asarray(removed, dtype=np.int64)] = False\n137\t    th = fit_bradley_terry(ctx[\"a\"][keep], ctx[\"b\"][keep], ctx[\"s\"][keep], ctx[\"m\"], ctx[\"ridge\"],\n138\t                           ctx[\"theta0\"] if theta_start is None else theta_start)\n139\t    margin = float(th[ctx[\"lo\"]] - th[ctx[\"hi\"]])\n140\t    return margin > MARGIN, margin, th\n141\t\n142\t\n143\tdef random_removal_baseline(ctx, k, rng):\n144\t    \"\"\"Control: does removing k uniformly random rows flip the pair (exact refit)?\"\"\"\n145\t    k = int(min(k, ctx[\"n\"]))\n146\t    rows = rng.choice(ctx[\"n\"], size=k, replace=False)\n147\t    return verify_by_refit(ctx, rows)[0]\n148\t\n149\t\n150\tdef _min_prefix(ctx, order, stop_at, known_flip=False):\n151\t    \"\"\"Smallest refit-verified prefix of ``order`` (bisection); None if the full order does not flip.\"\"\"\n152\t    order = np.asarray(order, dtype=np.int64)\n153\t    top = min(ctx[\"cap\"], len(order))\n154\t    if top < 1:\n155\t        return None\n156\t    if not known_flip and (time.monotonic() > stop_at or not verify_by_refit(ctx, order[:top])[0]):\n157\t        return None\n158\t    lo_k, hi_k = 0, top\n159\t    while hi_k - lo_k > 1 and time.monotonic() < stop_at:\n160\t        mid = (lo_k + hi_k) // 2\n161\t        if verify_by_refit(ctx, order[:mid])[0]:\n162\t            hi_k = mid\n163\t        else:\n164\t            lo_k = mid\n165\t    return order[:hi_k]\n166\t\n167\t\n168\tdef _relinearize(ctx, base, stop_at, limit):\n169\t    \"\"\"Re-linearised greedy starting from removed set ``base``; None if it needs more than ``limit`` rows.\"\"\"\n170\t    a, b, s, m, ridge, hi, lo = (ctx[k] for k in (\"a\", \"b\", \"s\", \"m\", \"ridge\", \"hi\", \"lo\"))\n171\t    keep = np.ones(ctx[\"n\"], bool)\n172\t    removed = [int(i) for i in base]\n173\t    if removed:\n174\t        keep[removed] = False\n175\t    flipped, margin, theta = verify_by_refit(ctx, removed)\n176\t    while not flipped:\n177\t        if time.monotonic() > stop_at or len(removed) >= limit:\n178\t            return None\n179\t        rows = np.flatnonzero(keep)\n180\t        g = influence_on_gap(a[rows], b[rows], s[rows], theta, hi, lo, m, ridge)\n181\t        order = np.argsort(g, kind=\"stable\")\n182\t        gs = g[order]\n183\t        neg = int(np.searchsorted(gs, 0.0))\n184\t        if neg == 0:\n185\t            return None\n186\t        red = -np.cumsum(gs[:neg])\n187\t        need = MARGIN - margin  # current gap theta_hi - theta_lo plus safety margin\n188\t        n_lin = min(int(np.searchsorted(red, need)) + 1, neg)\n189\t        batch = min(max(1, int(math.ceil(SHRINK * n_lin))), limit - len(removed))\n190\t        take = rows[order[:batch]]\n191\t        keep[take] = False\n192\t        removed.extend(int(i) for i in take)\n193\t        flipped, margin, theta = verify_by_refit(ctx, removed, theta)\n194\t    return _min_prefix(ctx, np.asarray(removed, dtype=np.int64), stop_at, known_flip=True)\n195\t\n196\t\n197\tdef _polish(ctx, best, stop_at):\n198\t    \"\"\"Drop-and-readd local search: drop the least useful rows of the incumbent, greedily refill.\"\"\"\n199\t    frac = 0.25\n200\t    for _ in range(14):\n201\t        if len(best) <= 1 or time.monotonic() > stop_at:\n202\t            break\n203\t        d = max(1, int(round(frac * len(best))))\n204\t        _, _, theta = verify_by_refit(ctx, best)\n205\t        infl = influence_on_gap(ctx[\"a\"], ctx[\"b\"], ctx[\"s\"], theta, ctx[\"hi\"], ctx[\"lo\"], ctx[\"m\"], ctx[\"ridge\"])\n206\t        useful_first = np.argsort(infl[best], kind=\"stable\")\n207\t        base = best[useful_first[:len(best) - d]]\n208\t        cand = _relinearize(ctx, base, stop_at, limit=len(best) - 1)\n209\t        if cand is not None and len(cand) < len(best):\n210\t            best = cand\n211\t        else:\n212\t            if d == 1:\n213\t                break\n214\t            frac *= 0.5\n215\t    return best\n216\t\n217\t\n218\tdef greedy_flip_budget(ctx, stop_at):\n219\t    \"\"\"Smallest refit-verified removal set found by influence-guided greedy search (None if none).\"\"\"\n220\t    n, cap = ctx[\"n\"], ctx[\"cap\"]\n221\t    infl0 = influence_on_gap(ctx[\"a\"], ctx[\"b\"], ctx[\"s\"], ctx[\"theta0\"], ctx[\"hi\"], ctx[\"lo\"], ctx[\"m\"],\n222\t                             ctx[\"ridge\"])\n223\t    best = _min_prefix(ctx, np.argsort(infl0, kind=\"stable\")[:cap], stop_at)\n224\t    cand = _relinearize(ctx, np.zeros(0, dtype=np.int64), stop_at, limit=(len(best) - 1 if best is not None else cap))\n225\t    if cand is not None and (best is None or len(cand) < len(best)):\n226\t        best = cand\n227\t    if best is not None:\n228\t        best = _polish(ctx, np.asarray(best, dtype=np.int64), stop_at)\n229\t    return best\n230\t\n231\t\n232\tdef _analyze(req, st):\n233\t    t_start = time.monotonic()\n234\t    a = np.concatenate([c[0] for c in st[\"chunks\"]]).astype(np.int64)\n235\t    b = np.concatenate([c[1] for c in st[\"chunks\"]]).astype(np.int64)\n236\t    y = np.concatenate([c[2] for c in st[\"chunks\"]])\n237\t    n, m = len(y), int(st[\"n_models\"])\n238\t    ridge = float(req[\"ridge\"])\n239\t    s = _scores(y) if req.get(\"tie_as_half_win\", True) else np.where(y == 0, 1.0, 0.0)\n240\t    hi, lo, cap = int(req[\"hi\"]), int(req[\"lo\"]), int(req[\"k_cap\"])\n241\t    stop_at = t_start + 0.6 * float(req[\"deadline_seconds\"])\n242\t    theta0 = fit_bradley_terry(a, b, s, m, ridge)\n243\t    ctx = {\"a\": a, \"b\": b, \"s\": s, \"n\": n, \"m\": m, \"ridge\": ridge, \"hi\": hi, \"lo\": lo, \"cap\": cap,\n244\t           \"theta0\": theta0, \"refits\": 0}\n245\t    best = greedy_flip_budget(ctx, stop_at)\n246\t    chosen = np.zeros(0, dtype=np.int64) if best is None else np.asarray(best, dtype=np.int64)[:cap]\n247\t    diag = {\"refits\": float(ctx[\"refits\"]), \"k\": float(len(chosen))}\n248\t    if len(chosen) and time.monotonic() < t_start + 0.8 * float(req[\"deadline_seconds\"]):\n249\t        diag[\"random_flip\"] = float(random_removal_baseline(ctx, len(chosen), st[\"rng\"]))\n250\t    return {\"removed\": _encode_u32(chosen), \"diagnostics\": diag}\n251\t\n252\t\n253\tdef handle(request):\n254\t    op = request.get(\"op\")\n255\t    if op == \"reset\":\n256\t        _STATE.clear()\n257\t        _STATE.update(_fresh(request[\"seed\"]))\n258\t        return {\"ok\": True}\n259\t    if not _STATE:\n260\t        raise RuntimeError(\"reset required\")\n261\t    if op == \"load_chunk\":\n262\t        a = _decode(request[\"a\"], np.uint16)\n263\t        b = _decode(request[\"b\"], np.uint16, len(a))\n264\t        y = _decode(request[\"y\"], np.uint8, len(a))\n265\t        if request[\"chunk_index\"] != len(_STATE[\"chunks\"]):\n266\t            raise ValueError(\"chunk out of order\")\n267\t        _STATE[\"chunks\"].append((a, b, y))\n268\t        _STATE.update(n_chunks=request[\"n_chunks\"], n_rows=request[\"n_rows_total\"], n_models=request[\"n_models\"])\n269\t        return {\"ok\": True}\n270\t    if op == \"analyze\":\n271\t        if len(_STATE[\"chunks\"]) != _STATE[\"n_chunks\"]:\n272\t            raise ValueError(\"table incomplete\")\n273\t        return _analyze(req=request, st=_STATE)\n274\t    raise ValueError(\"unknown op\")\n275\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69025aa5-9399-474f-82bf-b38cf111820f","uuid":"2929e340-3e25-4f8c-98d1-09f3c00d925c","timestamp":"2026-11-11T07:59:56.160Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/paper/source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py","content":"\"\"\"Influence-guided minimal-removal search for Bradley-Terry leaderboard rank flips.\n\nThe evaluator calls ``handle(request) -> response`` once per operation with finite JSON values.\nOne episode is: ``reset`` -> ``load_chunk`` x n_chunks -> ``analyze``. Every request is a dict with\nan ``op`` key; every response is a dict. All state lives in this process's memory. The evaluator\nand this process share no filesystem; never rely on paths.\n\nOperations\n----------\n{\"op\": \"reset\", \"seed\": int}\n    Clear ALL state (table, caches, RNG) and seed the RNG. Response: exactly {\"ok\": true}.\n\n{\"op\": \"load_chunk\", \"chunk_index\": int, \"n_chunks\": int, \"n_rows_total\": int, \"n_models\": int,\n \"a\": ARR, \"b\": ARR, \"y\": ARR}\n    One slice of the comparison table (in order, <= 65536 rows per chunk, <= 4 chunks). Row j is\n    \"model a[j] vs model b[j]\" with outcome y[j]: 0 = A wins, 1 = B wins, 2 = tie. ARR =\n    {\"dtype\": \"uint16\" | \"uint8\", \"shape\": [n], \"encoding\": \"base64-le\", \"data\": <base64>}.\n    Response: exactly {\"ok\": true}.\n\n{\"op\": \"analyze\", \"hi\": int, \"lo\": int, \"k_cap\": int, \"tie_as_half_win\": true, \"ridge\": float,\n \"deadline_seconds\": float}\n    Bradley-Terry logistic MLE with ridge; ``hi`` is ranked directly above ``lo``. Propose at most\n    ``k_cap`` unique row indices whose removal makes the exact refit rank ``lo`` strictly above\n    ``hi``. Score = 1 - k / k_cap if the refit flips, else 0.\n    Response: {\"removed\": {\"dtype\": \"uint32\", \"shape\": [k], \"encoding\": \"base64-le\", \"data\": ...},\n    \"diagnostics\": {<name>: <finite number>, ...}}  (optional, <= 32 numbers, ignored for scoring).\n\nMethod (this candidate)\n-----------------------\n1. ``fit_bradley_terry``: damped Newton with analytic gradient / dense Hessian.\n2. ``influence_on_gap``: one-step Newton (influence-function) effect of deleting each row on the\n   gap theta_hi - theta_lo, with the leave-one-out leverage correction 1/(1 - w_i x_i' H^-1 x_i).\n3. ``greedy_flip_budget``: (a) one-shot influence ranking + refit-verified prefix bisection;\n   (b) re-linearised greedy: after every batch refit and recompute influences, batch size = a\n   fraction of the linearised remaining need (Newton-like geometric convergence), then prefix\n   bisection over insertion order; (c) polish by drop-and-readd local search (drop the least useful\n   rows of the incumbent, re-run (b) with a strictly smaller size limit).\n4. ``verify_by_refit``: every candidate set is accepted only after an exact refit flips the pair by\n   a small safety margin. ``random_removal_baseline`` is the random-removal control (diagnostic only).\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\nimport math\nimport time\n\nimport numpy as np\n\n_STATE = {}\n\nMARGIN = 1e-5  # safety margin on theta_lo - theta_hi in our own exact refit\nSHRINK = 0.6  # fraction of the linearised need removed per re-linearised round\n\n\ndef _fresh(seed):\n    return {\"seed\": int(seed), \"rng\": np.random.default_rng(int(seed)), \"chunks\": [], \"n_chunks\": None,\n            \"n_rows\": None, \"n_models\": None}\n\n\ndef _decode(arr, dtype, n_expected=None):\n    if (type(arr) is not dict or arr.get(\"encoding\") != \"base64-le\" or arr.get(\"dtype\") != np.dtype(dtype).name):\n        raise ValueError(\"bad array\")\n    out = np.frombuffer(base64.b64decode(arr[\"data\"]), dtype=np.dtype(dtype).newbyteorder(\"<\"))\n    if list(arr[\"shape\"]) != [len(out)] or (n_expected is not None and len(out) != n_expected):\n        raise ValueError(\"bad shape\")\n    return out\n\n\ndef _encode_u32(idx):\n    idx = np.asarray(idx, dtype=\"<u4\")\n    return {\"dtype\": \"uint32\", \"shape\": [int(len(idx))], \"encoding\": \"base64-le\",\n            \"data\": base64.b64encode(idx.tobytes()).decode(\"ascii\")}\n\n\ndef _scores(y):\n    return np.where(y == 0, 1.0, np.where(y == 1, 0.0, 0.5))\n\n\ndef _hessian(a, b, w, m, ridge):\n    h = np.bincount(a * m + b, w, m * m).reshape(m, m)\n    h = -(h + h.T)\n    h[np.diag_indices(m)] += np.bincount(a, w, m) + np.bincount(b, w, m) + ridge\n    return h\n\n\ndef fit_bradley_terry(a, b, s, m, ridge, theta0=None, tol=1e-9, max_iter=60):\n    \"\"\"Ridge-regularised Bradley-Terry MLE (ties = half wins via s) by damped Newton.\"\"\"\n    th = np.zeros(m) if theta0 is None else theta0.copy()\n\n    def obj(t):\n        d = t[a] - t[b]\n        return float(np.sum(np.logaddexp(0.0, d) - s * d) + 0.5 * ridge * float(t @ t))\n\n    f = obj(th)\n    for _ in range(max_iter):\n        p = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-(th[a] - th[b])))\n        r = p - s\n        g = np.bincount(a, r, m) - np.bincount(b, r, m) + ridge * th\n        if np.max(np.abs(g)) < tol:\n            break\n        h = _hessian(a, b, p * (1.0 - p), m, ridge)\n        step = np.linalg.solve(h, g)\n        t = 1.0\n        while True:\n            fn = obj(th - t * step)\n            if fn <= f + 1e-12 * abs(f) or t < 1e-6:\n                break\n            t *= 0.5\n        th = th - t * step\n        f = fn\n    return th\n\n\ndef influence_on_gap(a, b, s, theta, hi, lo, m, ridge, leverage=True):\n    \"\"\"Newton-step change of theta[hi]-theta[lo] if each row were deleted (negative closes the gap).\"\"\"\n    p = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-(theta[a] - theta[b])))\n    w = p * (1.0 - p)\n    h = _hessian(a, b, w, m, ridge)\n    e = np.zeros(m)\n    e[hi], e[lo] = 1.0, -1.0\n    if leverage:\n        hinv = np.linalg.inv(h)\n        v = hinv @ e\n        d = np.diag(hinv)\n        q = d[a] + d[b] - 2.0 * hinv[a, b]\n        den = np.maximum(1.0 - w * q, 1e-3)\n    else:\n        v = np.linalg.solve(h, e)\n        den = 1.0\n    return (p - s) * (v[a] - v[b]) / den\n\n\ndef verify_by_refit(ctx, removed, theta_start=None):\n    \"\"\"Exact refit without ``removed``; returns (flipped, margin = theta_lo - theta_hi, theta).\"\"\"\n    ctx[\"refits\"] += 1\n    keep = np.ones(ctx[\"n\"], bool)\n    if len(removed):\n        keep[np.asarray(removed, dtype=np.int64)] = False\n    th = fit_bradley_terry(ctx[\"a\"][keep], ctx[\"b\"][keep], ctx[\"s\"][keep], ctx[\"m\"], ctx[\"ridge\"],\n                           ctx[\"theta0\"] if theta_start is None else theta_start)\n    margin = float(th[ctx[\"lo\"]] - th[ctx[\"hi\"]])\n    return margin > MARGIN, margin, th\n\n\ndef random_removal_baseline(ctx, k, rng):\n    \"\"\"Control: does removing k uniformly random rows flip the pair (exact refit)?\"\"\"\n    k = int(min(k, ctx[\"n\"]))\n    rows = rng.choice(ctx[\"n\"], size=k, replace=False)\n    return verify_by_refit(ctx, rows)[0]\n\n\ndef _min_prefix(ctx, order, stop_at, known_flip=False):\n    \"\"\"Smallest refit-verified prefix of ``order`` (bisection); None if the full order does not flip.\"\"\"\n    order = np.asarray(order, dtype=np.int64)\n    top = min(ctx[\"cap\"], len(order))\n    if top < 1:\n        return None\n    if not known_flip and (time.monotonic() > stop_at or not verify_by_refit(ctx, order[:top])[0]):\n        return None\n    lo_k, hi_k = 0, top\n    while hi_k - lo_k > 1 and time.monotonic() < stop_at:\n        mid = (lo_k + hi_k) // 2\n        if verify_by_refit(ctx, order[:mid])[0]:\n            hi_k = mid\n        else:\n            lo_k = mid\n    return order[:hi_k]\n\n\ndef _relinearize(ctx, base, stop_at, limit):\n    \"\"\"Re-linearised greedy starting from removed set ``base``; None if it needs more than ``limit`` rows.\"\"\"\n    a, b, s, m, ridge, hi, lo = (ctx[k] for k in (\"a\", \"b\", \"s\", \"m\", \"ridge\", \"hi\", \"lo\"))\n    keep = np.ones(ctx[\"n\"], bool)\n    removed = [int(i) for i in base]\n    if removed:\n        keep[removed] = False\n    flipped, margin, theta = verify_by_refit(ctx, removed)\n    while not flipped:\n        if time.monotonic() > stop_at or len(removed) >= limit:\n            return None\n        rows = np.flatnonzero(keep)\n        g = influence_on_gap(a[rows], b[rows], s[rows], theta, hi, lo, m, ridge)\n        order = np.argsort(g, kind=\"stable\")\n        gs = g[order]\n        neg = int(np.searchsorted(gs, 0.0))\n        if neg == 0:\n            return None\n        red = -np.cumsum(gs[:neg])\n        need = MARGIN - margin  # current gap theta_hi - theta_lo plus safety margin\n        n_lin = min(int(np.searchsorted(red, need)) + 1, neg)\n        batch = min(max(1, int(math.ceil(SHRINK * n_lin))), limit - len(removed))\n        take = rows[order[:batch]]\n        keep[take] = False\n        removed.extend(int(i) for i in take)\n        flipped, margin, theta = verify_by_refit(ctx, removed, theta)\n    return _min_prefix(ctx, np.asarray(removed, dtype=np.int64), stop_at, known_flip=True)\n\n\ndef _polish(ctx, best, stop_at):\n    \"\"\"Drop-and-readd local search: drop the least useful rows of the incumbent, greedily refill.\"\"\"\n    frac = 0.25\n    for _ in range(14):\n        if len(best) <= 1 or time.monotonic() > stop_at:\n            break\n        d = max(1, int(round(frac * len(best))))\n        _, _, theta = verify_by_refit(ctx, best)\n        infl = influence_on_gap(ctx[\"a\"], ctx[\"b\"], ctx[\"s\"], theta, ctx[\"hi\"], ctx[\"lo\"], ctx[\"m\"], ctx[\"ridge\"])\n        useful_first = np.argsort(infl[best], kind=\"stable\")\n        base = best[useful_first[:len(best) - d]]\n        cand = _relinearize(ctx, base, stop_at, limit=len(best) - 1)\n        if cand is not None and len(cand) < len(best):\n            best = cand\n        else:\n            if d == 1:\n                break\n            frac *= 0.5\n    return best\n\n\ndef greedy_flip_budget(ctx, stop_at):\n    \"\"\"Smallest refit-verified removal set found by influence-guided greedy search (None if none).\"\"\"\n    n, cap = ctx[\"n\"], ctx[\"cap\"]\n    infl0 = influence_on_gap(ctx[\"a\"], ctx[\"b\"], ctx[\"s\"], ctx[\"theta0\"], ctx[\"hi\"], ctx[\"lo\"], ctx[\"m\"],\n                             ctx[\"ridge\"])\n    best = _min_prefix(ctx, np.argsort(infl0, kind=\"stable\")[:cap], stop_at)\n    cand = _relinearize(ctx, np.zeros(0, dtype=np.int64), stop_at, limit=(len(best) - 1 if best is not None else cap))\n    if cand is not None and (best is None or len(cand) < len(best)):\n        best = cand\n    if best is not None:\n        best = _polish(ctx, np.asarray(best, dtype=np.int64), stop_at)\n    return best\n\n\ndef _analyze(req, st):\n    t_start = time.monotonic()\n    a = np.concatenate([c[0] for c in st[\"chunks\"]]).astype(np.int64)\n    b = np.concatenate([c[1] for c in st[\"chunks\"]]).astype(np.int64)\n    y = np.concatenate([c[2] for c in st[\"chunks\"]])\n    n, m = len(y), int(st[\"n_models\"])\n    ridge = float(req[\"ridge\"])\n    s = _scores(y) if req.get(\"tie_as_half_win\", True) else np.where(y == 0, 1.0, 0.0)\n    hi, lo, cap = int(req[\"hi\"]), int(req[\"lo\"]), int(req[\"k_cap\"])\n    stop_at = t_start + 0.6 * float(req[\"deadline_seconds\"])\n    theta0 = fit_bradley_terry(a, b, s, m, ridge)\n    ctx = {\"a\": a, \"b\": b, \"s\": s, \"n\": n, \"m\": m, \"ridge\": ridge, \"hi\": hi, \"lo\": lo, \"cap\": cap,\n           \"theta0\": theta0, \"refits\": 0}\n    best = greedy_flip_budget(ctx, stop_at)\n    chosen = np.zeros(0, dtype=np.int64) if best is None else np.asarray(best, dtype=np.int64)[:cap]\n    diag = {\"refits\": float(ctx[\"refits\"]), \"k\": float(len(chosen))}\n    if len(chosen) and time.monotonic() < t_start + 0.8 * float(req[\"deadline_seconds\"]):\n        diag[\"random_flip\"] = float(random_removal_baseline(ctx, len(chosen), st[\"rng\"]))\n    return {\"removed\": _encode_u32(chosen), \"diagnostics\": diag}\n\n\ndef handle(request):\n    op = request.get(\"op\")\n    if op == \"reset\":\n        _STATE.clear()\n        _STATE.update(_fresh(request[\"seed\"]))\n        return {\"ok\": True}\n    if not _STATE:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"reset required\")\n    if op == \"load_chunk\":\n        a = _decode(request[\"a\"], np.uint16)\n        b = _decode(request[\"b\"], np.uint16, len(a))\n        y = _decode(request[\"y\"], np.uint8, len(a))\n        if request[\"chunk_index\"] != len(_STATE[\"chunks\"]):\n            raise ValueError(\"chunk out of order\")\n        _STATE[\"chunks\"].append((a, b, y))\n        _STATE.update(n_chunks=request[\"n_chunks\"], n_rows=request[\"n_rows_total\"], n_models=request[\"n_models\"])\n        return {\"ok\": True}\n    if op == \"analyze\":\n        if len(_STATE[\"chunks\"]) != _STATE[\"n_chunks\"]:\n            raise ValueError(\"table incomplete\")\n        return _analyze(req=request, st=_STATE)\n    raise ValueError(\"unknown op\")\n","numLines":275,"startLine":1,"totalLines":275}}}
